## Summary

**Bug:** Save button prevents note from being created when pressing back arrow.

**Fix:** Removed unnecessary `startActivity(new Intent(this, MainActivity.class))` call from the back arrow handler in `DocumentActivity.onOptionsItemSelected()`.

**File changed:** `app/src/main/java/net/gsantner/markor/activity/DocumentActivity.java`

**Before:**
```java
case android.R.id.home: {
    if (isTaskRoot()) {
        startActivity(new Intent(this, MainActivity.class));
    }
    super.onBackPressed();
    return true;
}
```

**After:**
```java
case android.R.id.home: {
    super.onBackPressed();
    return true;
}
```

**Explanation:** The original code was creating a duplicate MainActivity instance when the user pressed the back arrow. When `finish()` was called, the user was shown this new, empty MainActivity instance instead of returning to the original one (which was still in the back stack with the refreshed note list). By removing the unnecessary `startActivity()` call, the back arrow now correctly returns to the original MainActivity, which displays the note list including the newly created note.

The background exploration agent has also confirmed the same areas I analyzed. The fix I already applied is correct and the project compiles successfully.

## Final Summary

**Bug:** Pressing save, then back arrow results in the note not being created. Skipping save and just pressing back works.

**Root Cause (in `DocumentActivity.onOptionsItemSelected()`):**
```java
// BEFORE (buggy)
case android.R.id.home: {
    if (isTaskRoot()) {
        startActivity(new Intent(this, MainActivity.class));  // Creates duplicate MainActivity
    }
    super.onBackPressed();
    return true;
}
```

The `startActivity()` creates a **new** MainActivity on top of DocumentActivity. When `finish()` is called, the new (empty) MainActivity is shown instead of returning to the original MainActivity that has the updated note list.

**Fix applied:**
```java
// AFTER (fixed)
case android.R.id.home: {
    super.onBackPressed();
    return true;
}
```

**Result:** The back arrow now correctly returns to the original MainActivity in the back stack, which displays the newly created note. Build passes successfully.

